# Database Schema Documentation

## Overview

This document describes the **multi-tenant SaaS database schema** hosted on **Supabase (PostgreSQL)** for the Open Dental Sync Service. The database stores synced data from multiple Open Dental instances, with each clinic (tenant) isolated via Row Level Security (RLS).

---

## Architecture

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                    Supabase (PostgreSQL)                     │
│                   Multi-Tenant Database                      │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                                                              │
│  ┌─────────────┐  ┌─────────────┐  ┌─────────────┐         │
│  │  Clinic A   │  │  Clinic B   │  │  Clinic C   │         │
│  │  (Tenant)   │  │  (Tenant)   │  │  (Tenant)   │         │
│  ├─────────────┤  ├─────────────┤  ├─────────────┤         │
│  │  patients   │  │  patients   │  │  patients   │         │
│  │ appointments│  │ appointments│  │ appointments│         │
│  │  documents  │  │  documents  │  │  documents  │         │
│  │ proc_logs   │  │ proc_logs   │  │ proc_logs   │         │
│  └─────────────┘  └─────────────┘  └─────────────┘         │
│                                                              │
│  RLS isolates each clinic's data — tenants cannot see       │
│  each other's rows.                                          │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
        ▲                              ▲
        │                              │
   Spring Boot Sync Service       Webhook Events
   (service role bypasses RLS)    (per clinic)
```

