## Tables

### 1. `clinics` — Tenant Registry

**Purpose:** Registers each clinic (tenant) in the SaaS platform. Each clinic has its own Open Dental instance.

| Column | Type | Description |
|--------|------|-------------|
| `id` | UUID (PK) | Unique clinic identifier |
| `clinic_name` | text | Display name (e.g., "Clinic A - Downtown") |
| `clinic_code` | text (unique) | Short code (e.g., `CLINIC_A`) used in API paths |
| `base_url` | text | Open Dental API base URL for this clinic |
| `api_key` | text | Open Dental API key for authentication |
| `is_active` | boolean | Whether this clinic is active |
| `subscription_tier` | text | SaaS plan: `free`, `pro`, or `enterprise` |
| `max_patients` | integer | Patient limit for this tier |
| `webhook_secret` | text | Secret for verifying inbound webhooks |
| `last_sync_at` | timestamptz | Last successful reconciliation sync |
| `last_webhook_at` | timestamptz | Last webhook event received |
| `created_at` | timestamptz | Record creation time |
| `updated_at` | timestamptz | Last update time (auto-maintained) |

**Why it exists:** Without this table, the system cannot know which clinics exist, what their Open Dental URLs are, or how to authenticate with their Open Dental instances.

