### 6. Reference Data Tables (Tenant-Scoped)

These tables hold Open Dental lookups/reference data that the reconciliation
job reconciles from their webhooks: `pat_fields`, `providers`, `operatories`,
`schedules`, and `tooth_initials`.

**Primary Key Pattern:** every reference table uses `(clinic_id, <num>)` so each
tenant gets its own namespace of reference rows. `is_deleted`/`deleted_at`/
`deleted_by` columns power soft-deletion from the `*Deleted` webhooks and from
the reconciliation diff (a row present in Supabase but missing from Open Dental
is soft-deleted).

#### 6a. `pat_fields` — Patient Custom Fields

| Column | Type | Description |
|--------|------|-------------|
| `clinic_id` | UUID (PK part) | FK to `clinics.id` |
| `pat_field_num` | bigint (PK part) | Open Dental custom-field number |
| `pat_num` | bigint | FK to patients — which patient |
| `field_name` | text | Field name (e.g., PatStatus, DeletedDateTime) |
| `field_value` | text | Field value |
| `field_desc` | text | Field description |
| `field_type` | text | Field type |
| `clinic_num` | bigint | Open Dental clinic number |
| `deleted_by` | bigint | Who deleted the field (from PatFieldDeleted) |
| `deleted_at` | timestamp | When it was deleted |
| `is_deleted` | boolean | Soft-delete flag |
| `created_at` / `updated_at` | timestamptz | Audit timestamps |

**Why it exists:** Reconciles the `PatField` and `PatFieldDeleted` webhooks;
also carries patient lifecycle markers (PatStatus / DeletedDateTime /
DeletedByUserNum) used to update the linked patient.

