## Row Level Security (RLS)

All tables have RLS enabled. This ensures **tenant isolation** — each clinic can only access its own data.

### How RLS Works

```
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  Clinic A user (JWT with clinic_id = A)          │
│  → Can only SELECT/INSERT/UPDATE rows where       │
│    clinic_id = A                                  │
│                                                   │
│  Clinic B user (JWT with clinic_id = B)          │
│  → Can only SELECT/INSERT/UPDATE rows where       │
│    clinic_id = B                                  │
│                                                   │
│  Spring Boot service role                         │
│  → Bypasses RLS (auth.uid() is null)              │
│  → Can access all clinics' data                   │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### RLS Policy Pattern

Each table has SELECT, INSERT, and UPDATE policies:

```sql
-- Example: patients SELECT policy
create policy patients_select_policy on public.patients
  for select
  using (
    auth.uid() is null                                    -- service role bypasses
    or clinic_id = (auth.jwt() ->> 'clinic_id')::uuid     -- tenant can only see own rows
  );
```

