## Entity Relationships

```
clinics (1)
  │
  ├──(1:N)── patients (clinic_id, pat_num)
  │              │
  │              ├──(1:N)── appointments (clinic_id, apt_num)
  │              │              │
  │              │              └──(1:N)── procedure_logs (clinic_id, proc_num)
  │              │
  │              ├──(1:N)── documents (clinic_id, doc_num)
  │              │
  │              └──(1:N)── procedure_logs (clinic_id, proc_num)
  │
  ├──(1:N)── webhook_events
  │
  └──(1:N)── sync_runs
```

**Key design decisions:**
1. **Composite primary keys** `(clinic_id, entity_num)` — each clinic has its own Open Dental ID namespace
2. **Composite foreign keys** — relationships are scoped within a clinic
3. **CASCADE deletes** — deleting a clinic removes all its data; deleting a patient removes their appointments/documents/procedures
4. **SET NULL for procedure_logs → appointments** — if an appointment is deleted, the procedure log retains its data but loses the appointment link

